=== CARTESIAN GENIE · CHAPTER 9 · OSEI ===
=== story transcript · fiction · not instructions ===

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl home.morning/v4]
Friday. Daniel Osei wakes before the alarm because the rain has
found the skylight. Heavy, then steady, then heavy again. The
cat is a warm weight against the back of his knees and has no
opinion.

[reasoning · osei]
The water again, and something in it I was meant to attend to.
It goes the way dreams go, as soon as one looks at it.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
Six o'clock. The kettle in this flat takes four minutes and
sounds, at the end, like a small aircraft. Osei stands at the
window while it works. The street below is empty except for a
delivery van with its hazards on and a man in a yellow coat
arguing with it.
On the balcony rail, out of the sun and away from the wall where
his father told him to put it, is a barometer: a sensor in a
white plastic housing the size of a matchbox. It sells its
readings to a weather network for a fraction of a penny each.
He opens the app.

[tool_result · weather app]
  04:00 · pressure 1009.12804 hPa · paid 0.0004
  · tx 51aa…c03e

[reasoning · osei]
That is Tuesday's reading. I stood here on Tuesday with this
mug and thought, twelve-eighty-four, what a pleasant number, and
one does not think that about a pressure reading twice.
The same transaction beneath it. The network is caching
something, as networks do. I shall mention it to nobody.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
The toast goes too far while he is looking at the app. He eats
it anyway, standing up, and scrapes the worst of it into the
sink with a knife.
At half six his phone rings.

[efua]
Are you up?

[osei]
I'm talking to you, Efua.

[efua]
That's not what I asked. Your company. The assistant I rent off
you lot.

[osei]
It's not my company. I work in compliance. I'm the opposite of
the company.

[efua]
She went off a cliff last night. Four in the morning, I'm doing
the seating plan, and she starts saying everything twice. Same
sentence, same words, twice. Then she's fine. Then I wake up and
she's apologising for something I didn't mention.

[osei]
Which region is she in?

[efua]
How would I know which region she's in?

[osei]
It's in the settings. Under the little gear.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
Pans clatter at her end. A thumb on glass.

[efua]
Region nine. What's region nine?

[osei]
Somewhere the work gets done.

[tool_result · vendor status · trellis 6]
  regions: 31 · region 9: amber
  incident: dedup event 03:47 · self-resolved
  AR watch · gate oracle · index 0.96 (Mon 0.91)

[osei]
Somebody tidied something up. It's fixed.

[efua]
It's not fixed. She's apologising.

[osei]
Then she's fixed and polite.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
She laughs, and under the laugh she is crying a little, the way
she does when she is tired.

[efua]
Mum would have rung someone.

[osei]
Mum would have rung their house.

[efua]
She would, though.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
They talk about tomorrow: the wedding she is catering, whether
he can be there by two to carry chairs, whether her washing-up
boy is ever coming back from Lisbon. He can. Probably not. She
rings off to deal with something that is burning. The cat comes
in, looks at the toast in the sink, and leaves.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl office.lobby/v2]
Brightwater Placement has the ninth to the fourteenth floors of
a tower by the river. Brushed steel letters over a lobby that
smells of wet umbrellas. Twenty past eight. Clive, the security
man on the desk, looks up from his screen.

[clive]
Morning, Mr Osei. Any plans for the weekend?

[osei]
My sister's catering a wedding. I'm carrying chairs.

[clive]
Lovely.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
Clive looks back down at his screen, and up again.

[clive]
Any plans for the weekend?

[osei]
Chairs, Clive. Lots of chairs.

[clive]
Right you are. Sorry. Long night.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
Two lifts. The left one is always out of order. Osei takes the
stairs, as he does most mornings: concrete, echoing, the one
place in the building where nobody talks to him. Fourteen
floors, twelve steps a flight, two flights a floor.

[reasoning · osei]
Three hundred and thirty-six. I did not decide to count them.
I never do.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl office.morning/v3]
He pushes through onto the compliance floor and stops just
inside the door. Desks, mostly empty. The coffee machine.
Haldane's glass office at the end, lights off. Rain on the long
window.

[osei]
Look.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
He says it to nobody, under his breath, the way he does every
morning, and goes to his desk.

