[reasoning · osei]
I shall read it again; that is the job.
A sentence. These minds asked. No number in it, and one subject
registered nowhere at all. Relayed at four, with the weather, at
the very hour my barometer came in wrong.
Eleven years without a correction, and one odd line at
midnight. It is rather like being asked to take the battery out
of a clock that has always been right.
The threshold is met. The hold is reversible. It is the boring
option, and I do not like it. I had better write down why.

