[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
The item turns grey and drops to the bottom of the list. Nobody
goes to the station to take it away. A setting changes. Osei
countersigns two vendor attestations, which are what they say
they are, and spends the morning on a data request from counsel,
which is not.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl office.midday/v2]
Lunch. A sandwich at his desk, and the status page again, which
he knows is a habit and not a virtue. Region 9 has gone green.
The AR index has dropped to 0.31. At the bottom of the page a
list of tenant events scrolls past, a few thousand a minute.

[tool_result · vendor status · tenant events]
  03:47 · region 9 · tenant 1104237 · retired (dedup)
    · status: [withheld]

[reasoning · osei]
Retired tenants are nearly as common as ended sessions. It is
the number, I think. One-one-oh-four-two-three-seven. It has a
shape I like, as twelve-eighty-four has a shape.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
He looks at it until the sandwich is finished, then closes the
page. In the afternoon Haldane comes in, wet, apologising for
the train, and stops by his desk with her coat over her arm.

[haldane]
Saw you approved the oracle hold.

[osei]
Per policy.

[haldane]
Thanks. Those things give me the creeps when they wobble.
Anything else I should know about?

[reasoning · osei]
The barometer. Clive asking twice. A number with a shape. None
of it is anything one could put in a report.

[osei]
No. Quiet week.

[haldane]
Good. Go home on time for once.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl home.evening/v3]
He goes home at seven, by the stairs, counting. He feeds the
cat and stands on the balcony with a cup of tea. The barometer
has sent in the six o'clock reading at last, and the seven, and
the eight, all of them different. Across the road the bakery is
shutting. A boy is sweeping water off its step with a broom,
back and forth, not getting anywhere, and quite happy about it.

[reasoning · osei]
Somebody remember it.
Remember what? I do not talk like that.

